# Root ignore rules for the Acme supplier onboarding monorepo.
#
# backend/.gitignore and frontend/.gitignore already cover their own build
# artifacts. This file covers what crosses both: operating-system noise, editor
# state, and — the part that matters — anything whose leak would be an incident.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and credentials
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# This system holds tax and banking documents, and the client explicitly said a
# past vendor was careless with sensitive data. These patterns are deliberately
# broad: a false positive costs a `git add -f`, a false negative costs a
# credential rotation and an awkward conversation.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Google Cloud service account keys. CI authenticates through Workload Identity
# Federation precisely so these never need to exist, but a key downloaded during
# debugging must not be one `git add .` away from the history.
*service-account*.json
*service_account*.json
*-sa.json
gcp-key*.json
application_default_credentials.json

# Spring profile overrides. `application.yml` is committed and holds only
# non-secret defaults; anything ending in -local or -secret is for a developer's
# own machine.
**/application-local.yml
**/application-local.yaml
**/application-secret*.yml
**/application-secret*.yaml

# Keys, certificates and keystores in any form.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local data
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The local filesystem storage adapter writes uploaded documents here. In a
# seeded environment that means W-9s and banking forms sitting in the working
# tree — never commit it.
.local-storage/

# Docker volume data, if a bind mount is ever used instead of a named volume.
.postgres-data/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Operating system
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and tooling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

.idea/
*.iml
*.iws
*.ipr

.vscode/*
# Shared editor recommendations are useful to commit; personal settings are not.
!.vscode/extensions.json

# Claude Code: shared project settings are committed, per-developer overrides
# are not.
.claude/settings.local.json

*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build and dependency output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Duplicated from the subproject ignore files on purpose: a root-level net still
# catches these if a directory is ever moved or a new module is added.

node_modules/
dist/
build/
.gradle/
.kotlin/
out/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs and transient output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

*.log
firebase-debug.log*
firestore-debug.log*
.firebase/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ignored
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar  — the wrapper only guarantees a
#       reproducible build if it is committed.
#   frontend/src/api/                  — the generated OpenAPI client is
#       committed so the frontend builds without a running backend. An evaluator
#       cloning this repo should not need Postgres up to run `npm run build`.
#   docker-compose.yml, application.yml — non-secret defaults, and the compose
#       credentials are local-only throwaways.
